Q: Warning &quot;Don&#39;t use &#39;BuildContext&#39;s across async gaps&quot; A: <p>The warning appears because await controller.login(...) creates an async gap. During that time, the widget that owns this BuildContext might be removed from the widget tree (for example, if the user navigates back or closes the screen). After the await completes, you still use context for Navigator.push and ScaffoldMessenger.of(context), but if the widget has already been disposed, that context is no longer valid and can cause a crash, so the linter warns you.</p>
<p>In a StatefulWidget, you can fix this by checking mounted after the async call and before using context:</p>
<pre><code>void login() async {
  final success = await controller.login(_passwordController.text);

  if (!mounted) return;

  if (success) {
    Navigator.push(
      context,
      MaterialPageRoute(builder: (_) =&gt; const HomeScreen()),
    );
  } else {
    ScaffoldMessenger.of(context).showSnackBar(
      const SnackBar(content: Text(&quot;hello flutter&quot;)),
    );
  }
}
</code></pre>

Q: How to translate jquery ui datepicker in multiple language? A: <p>Then you can use:</p>

<pre><code>$( selector ).datepicker( $.datepicker.regional[ "en" ] );
$( selector ).datepicker( $.datepicker.regional[ "de" ] );
$( selector ).datepicker( $.datepicker.regional[ "nl" ] );
$( selector ).datepicker( $.datepicker.regional[ "fr" ] );
</code></pre>

<p>Something dynamic could be using a jQuery variable:</p>

<pre><code>var languages = "en","fr";

 $( selector ).datepicker( $.datepicker.regional[ +languages+ ] );
</code></pre>
